# ATM UML State Diagram
This file (`atm_state_diagram.dot`) represents the UML State Machine Diagram for an ATM.

## How to View the Diagram
- Use [Edotor](https://edotor.net/) or [Graphviz Online](https://dreampuf.github.io/GraphvizOnline/)
- Or run:
digraph ATM_State_Diagram {
    rankdir=LR;
    node [shape=rectangle];

    Start [shape=circle, label="Start"];
    PIN_Entry [label="PIN Entry\nentry/Prompt User"];
    Validate_PIN [label="Validate PIN\nentry/Check PIN\nexit/Increment Attempt Counter (if incorrect)"];
    Reject [shape=doublecircle, label="Reject Customer"];
    Select_Transaction [label="Select Transaction\nentry/Display Options"];
    Check_Balance [label="Check Balance\nentry/Fetch Account Balance\nexit/Authorize Transaction"];
    Withdraw [label="Withdraw Money\nentry/Verify Funds\nexit/Deduct Amount"];
    Deposit [label="Deposit Money\nentry/Accept Funds\nexit/Update Balance"];
    Transfer [label="Transfer Funds\nentry/Verify Accounts\nexit/Complete Transfer"];
    Print_Receipt [label="Print Receipt\nentry/Generate Statement"];
    End [shape=doublecircle, label="End Transaction"];

    Start -> PIN_Entry [label="Insert Card"];
    PIN_Entry -> Validate_PIN [label="Enter PIN"];
    Validate_PIN -> Reject [label="Enter PIN [Incorrect && Max Attempts Reached] / Reject Customer"];
    Validate_PIN -> Select_Transaction [label="Enter PIN [Correct] / Grant Access"];
    Select_Transaction -> Check_Balance [label="Withdraw or Transfer / Fetch Balance"];
    Select_Transaction -> Deposit [label="Deposit / Accept Funds"];
    Check_Balance -> Withdraw [label="Withdraw Request [Sufficient Balance] / Proceed with Withdrawal"];
    Check_Balance -> Reject [label="Withdraw Request [Insufficient Balance] / Reject Transaction"];
    Withdraw -> Print_Receipt [label="Transaction Complete / Print Receipt"];
    Deposit -> Print_Receipt [label="Transaction Complete / Print Receipt"];
    Transfer -> Print_Receipt [label="Transaction Complete / Print Receipt"];
    Print_Receipt -> End [label="Print Complete / End Session"];
}



